    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Channels by Test Card is an electronic release on Home Service Recordings that draws on the long British tradition of test-card and broadcast music. In that context, the album sits comfortably alongside the group’s broader fascination with the textures of television idents, interval signals, and library-style sounds, favoring atmosphere and timbre over conventional song structure.\n\nAs an electronic record, Channels is best understood as a set of mood pieces: carefully sequenced, finely detailed, and rooted in the kind of restrained, functional music that can feel both nostalgic and strangely futuristic. Its appeal lies in that tension between public-service utility and private listening, making it a fitting addition to a label and catalog associated with archival-minded electronic sound.",
